  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2be9535df9fadce4d9fc0e46ba83a908, type: 3}
  m_Name: Customer_GrannyRuby
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WeatherForSale.Shop.CustomerData
  displayName: Granny Ruby
  prefab: {fileID: 6424096899533240967, guid: e1165cf2123f94c42a1d833938789332, type: 3}
  weatherWord: snow
  correctMapId: glacier
  problemLine: My grandchild wants to feel real winter cold just once. In all my
    years, I've never seen snow either.
  hintsVague:
  - Something soft and white that floats down and makes the whole town quiet... that's
    all we wish for.
  - My grandchild keeps asking what it feels like when the sky sends down little
    white feathers.
  - I have knitted three woolly scarves and never once had a reason to wear them.
  hintsNarrow:
  - When I was a girl, I heard of peaks so cold that what lands on them never melts,
    not even in summer.
  - Travellers say the mountains there glitter blue and white, and the air bites
    your nose.
  - They say your breath turns into little clouds the moment you speak there.
  hintsClear:
  - My grandchild wants to build a little man with a carrot nose. Only the coldest,
    highest place will do.
  - Look for the tallest pointy mountains on your map, the ones with pale blue tops.
  - Pine trees wearing thick white coats, and tall cliffs that sparkle in the light.
  - On your map it's the top-right corner, where everything shimmers pale and blue.
  thankYouLine: Real snow... My grandchild will be so happy. Thank you, dear.
